From: shuuri-labs <61762328+shuuri-labs@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_fg: report charge current as positive

The gauge's current register counts discharge as positive, and CURRENT_NOW
passed it through, so the battery read +0.9 A on battery and -1.2 A while
charging. The power supply ABI counts charge as positive, and UPower calls
any battery with negative current discharging, so Steam showed the device
as not charging a moment after it was plugged in. Negate the reported
value; the driver's own current-based status fallback keeps the raw sign.
---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_fg.c
@@ -923,7 +923,14 @@
 		ret = chip->ops->get_capacity(chip, &val->intval);
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CURRENT_NOW:
-		ret = chip->ops->get_current(chip, &val->intval);
+		/*
+		 * The gauge counts discharge as positive; the ABI and UPower (which
+		 * calls negative current discharging) want charge positive. Negate
+		 * here only: the STATUS fallback above reads the raw sign.
+		 */
+		ret = chip->ops->get_current(chip, &temp);
+		if (!ret)
+			val->intval = -temp;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_VOLTAGE_NOW:
 		ret = chip->ops->get_voltage(chip, &val->intval);
